            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for chalk, then the Kannada for a ruler."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಪುರಾವೆ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪುರಾವೆ — purāve — \"proof; evidence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅವನ ಮಾತಿಗೆ ಯಾವುದೇ ಪುರಾವೆ ಇರಲಿಲ್ಲ. avana mātige yāvudē purāve iralilla. There was no proof for what he said."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With ಇದೆ and ಇಲ್ಲ: ಪುರಾವೆ (purāve) ಇದೆ, there is proof."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಪುರಾವೆ (purāve) has no entry in DEDR or CDIAL, so its origin is not settled. Marathi uses a close form, purāvā, for evidence."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for giving reasons and opinions."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
